    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d595">

                <pb facs="0825" n="723" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg723"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.84/432: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Ethiopia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">George</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Addis Ababa</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-07-04T12:00:00+02:35">July 4,
                            1935—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received July 4—6:42 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>52. Unexpectedly summoned to Palace last evening. Emperor gave me oral résumé of
                    events past 6 months concluding that since <pb facs="0826" n="724"
                        xml:id="pg724"/> Eden visit to Rome<anchor n="35" xml:id="d595-f1"/> Italy’s
                    intention conquest beyond doubt. Referring to last December’s exchange with
                    Department (see my telegram of Dec. 19, 10 a.m.<anchor n="36" xml:id="d595-f2"
                    />), Emperor declared he will continue to pursue Geneva procedure but feels it
                    his duty to ask American Government “to examine means of securing Italy’s
                    observance of engagements as signatory of the Kellogg Pact”. I had previously
                    mentioned and now repeated circumstances of 1931 invocation.<anchor n="37"
                        xml:id="d595-f3"/> Emperor’s oral statement immediately confirmed in writing
                    and being released to press.<anchor n="38" xml:id="d595-f4"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">George</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d595-f1" n="35" xml:id="d595-f1-content">
                <p>June 24–26. See statement by Anthony Eden in the House of Commons, Hansard, July
                    1, 1935, col. 1520–1522.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d595-f2" n="36" xml:id="d595-f2-content">
